  - title: A living river
    number: 3
    heartsNeeded: 3
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - My next exhibition is about the river as it used to be. Old maps, old photographs, old fishing nets.
    - But I want one living thing in the room. An eel, in a tank. Eels used to be everywhere in this valley. Now people do not believe they were ever here.
    - Could you catch one? Carefully. They are older and stranger than they look.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a3b6617a86c1c7846be723c7c8df372a, type: 2}
      amount: 1
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: An eel for the museum
      questText: Yuki wants an eel from the river for her exhibition about the valley as it used to be.
      reminder:
      - Any luck with an eel? They are shy. Fish at dusk, my father says. He is usually right about things that move slowly.
      thanks:
      - Look at it. Look at how it moves. Like ink in water.
      - It will have the best tank in the museum. And a label with your name on it, as the collector.
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 150
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Sterling & Sons
    number: 4
    heartsNeeded: 4
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags:
      - story_grace_4
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - Grace showed me the boot. 'Sterling & Sons Tannery.' Then we spent four hours in the museum basement with the archive boxes.
    - We found the tannery's own records. Every barrel of chrome, every load of lime. They wrote it all down, very neatly. They were proud of it.
    - I have never been so angry at good handwriting.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
