      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: After hours
    number: 7
    heartsNeeded: 7
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - Come to the museum tonight, after closing. I want to show you the exhibition as I made it. Before anyone changes it.
    - Here is the wetland, painted from Grace's maps. Here are the tannery records. Here is your eel, in the middle of everything, looking unimpressed.
    - And here is the last room. Empty, for now. I wanted it to be the valley as it could be again. I have not decided what to put in it.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Which room?
    number: 8
    heartsNeeded: 8
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - The museum director says I must choose. Remove the wetland section, or lose the sponsor, and possibly my job.
    - Or there is another way. The Kims' back room is empty in the evenings. I could take the whole exhibition there. Free. Small. Ours.
    - In the museum, ten thousand people would see it. In the suburb, a few hundred would. But nobody could tell me to take anything out.
    - My father says 'ask the farmer'. So I am asking the farmer.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 1
      optionA: Open it honestly at the museum
      replyA:
      - The museum, then, and all of it. If they take the sponsorship away, they take it away.
      - I will write the labels myself tonight. In very clear, very neat handwriting. The Sterlings taught me that.
      flagsA:
      - yuki_honest_exhibition
      - tower_file_tannery
      optionB: Move it to a pop-up in the suburb
      replyB:
      - A pop-up. Yes. Small and stubborn, like this street.
      - I will need Walt for the shelves, Lena for the signs, and you for carrying the eel. Very carefully.
      flagsB:
      - suburb_museum_open
      - tower_file_tannery
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Ten thousand people
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - The exhibition opened. The sponsor withdrew the same afternoon. The director shook my hand and said 'well done' in a voice that meant 'you're fired'.
    - But the city paper reviewed it. 'The most important room in the museum is the one about a swamp.' People queued.
    - Victor Sterling came on the second day. He stood in front of the tannery records for twenty minutes. Then he left without a word. That was the best review of all.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
